 "explanation": "The run class depends on counts of active neurons (100 <= active <= 7,667 and <= 1,022 above 100 Hz on the full cord). Inhibitory units with >= 100 members are 'ok' at every current because the stimulated members alone are active and they silence their targets; units with < 100 members that excite little stay 'weak'; excitatory units with many members already saturate at 128. The current changes the rates (neurons above 100 Hz rise with the current) without crossing a class boundary, except 01B (ok -> strong at 512) and 27X (weak -> ok in 4 of 8 seeds at 512)."
